  "rationale": "The workflow runs `python -m pip install --upgrade pip` and `pip install -r tests/requirements.txt` on every run with no dependency cache, so repeated runs re-fetch dependencies. The P-LIT-GHA-CACHE pattern (cache dependency downloads) is supported by the literature report (S01, sections 4.2.1/Table 4) and by the measured fork experiment showing pip-cache benefit. Adding an `actions/cache@v4` step for `~/.cache/pip`, keyed on `tests/requirements.txt` (the file that drives the install) with a restore-key prefix, preserves all build/test steps and coverage, requires no new privileges, secrets, deployment, or network access, and keeps `contents: read` permissions.",
